  "finding": {
    "verdict": "ISSUES #129's premise is FALSE. The stock ROM DOES spend a King's Rock Random() at MOVEEND_KINGSROCK_SHELLBELL on an OHKO KO. The engine (src/engine/battleScriptMoveEndOpcode.ts:883-905) was already source-exact; nothing needed porting.",
    "whyTheOldReceiptSaidOtherwise": "tools/battle-lab/gate6-ohko-hit-off.json's trace is 934 frames and stalls at frame 443. STRINGID_TARGETFAINTED ('Foe METAPOD fainted!\\p') ends in the 0xFB prompt control code, so BattleScript_FaintTarget's printstring (data/battle_scripts_1.s:2817-2823) leaves the player controller in CompleteOnInactiveTextPrinter with gBattleControllerExecFlags = 1 until a button is pressed. RunBattleScriptCommands only runs an opcode when gBattleControllerExecFlags == 0, so gBattlescriptCurrInstr sat on BattleScript_FaintTarget+12 (the `return` that pops back to `moveendall`) for the remaining 491 frames -- verified out to 3000 frames with no A press. Cmd_moveend therefore never executed inside the observed window and the receipt recorded 'no King's Rock draw' for a state that never ran.",
    "measuredFix": "The #129 fixtures are the gate6 hit fixture with 20 two-frame A pulses appended (tools/battle-lab/issue129-*.json). With them, gBattleScripting.moveendState is observed leaving 0: state 10 (MOVEEND_TARGET_VISIBLE) at frame 640, state 11 (MOVEEND_ITEM_EFFECTS_ALL) at 641, and state 17 (MOVEEND_COUNT) at 642 -- states 12..16 all run inside frame 642, and exactly ONE Random() lands in that frame.",
    "attributionControl": "arms.ohkoNoItemControl is the same fixture with the DUGTRIO's item forced to 0. It draws at frames 67 and 359 only: the frame-642 draw disappears with the item, so it is ItemBattleEffects's `(Random() % 100) < atkHoldEffectParam` (src/battle_util.c:3776) and nothing else. Of MOVEEND_KINGSROCK_SHELLBELL(12), MOVEEND_SUBSTITUTE(13), MOVEEND_UPDATE_LAST_MOVES(14), MOVEEND_MIRROR_MOVE(15), MOVEEND_NEXT_TARGET(16) (include/constants/battle_script_commands.h:402-408), only state 12 calls Random().",
    "guardStateAtStateEleven": "On the OHKO KO arm, immediately before state 12 runs: gBattleMoveDamage = 125, gSpecialStatuses[target].physicalDmg = 125 (TARGET_TURN_DAMAGED true, include/battle.h:469), gSpecialStatuses[target].shellBellDmg = 125, gMoveResultFlags = 0 (Cmd_resultmessage clears the flags after printing -- observed at frame 271, 20 -> 0), gBattlerAttacker = 0 holding item 187, gBattleMons[target].hp = 0. Every gate ahead of the draw is satisfied; only the trailing `&& gBattleMons[gBattlerTarget].hp` is false, and src/battle_util.c:3773-3780 evaluates it AFTER the draw. Nothing on this path ever zeroes gBattleMoveDamage: Cmd_tryfaintmon (src/battle_script_commands.c:2975-3049) and FaintClearSetData (src/battle_main.c:3264-3356) both leave it alone, and Cmd_getexp's `gBattleMoveDamage = 0` (:3349) runs later, from HandleFaintedMonActions.",
    "structOffsetsCited": "struct SpecialStatus (include/battle.h:132-147) is 20 bytes: +0 bitfield, +4 shellBellDmg, +8 physicalDmg, +12 specialDmg, +16/+17 battler ids. struct BattleScripting (include/battle.h:489-518): painSplitHp +0 (s32), bideDmg +4 (s32), multihitString[6] +8, dmgMultiplier +14, twoTurnsMoveStringId +15, animArg1 +16, animArg2 +17, tripleKickPower +18 (u16) => moveendState +20. struct BattlePokemon (include/pokemon.h:260-295): hp +0x28, maxHP +0x2C, item +0x2E, stride 0x58."
  },
  "scopeVerdict": {
    "kingsRock": "GENERIC, not OHKO-specific and not KO-specific. All three KING'S ROCK arms spend exactly one moveend draw: FISSURE OHKO KO (frame 642), EARTHQUAKE one-hit KO of a 4x-weak MAGNETON (frame 642), and a non-KO EARTHQUAKE on METAPOD that leaves it at 76/125 (frame 299). The draw follows every hit that set physicalDmg/specialDmg on the target, whatever the outcome.",
    "shellBell": "NOT suppressed by a KO. gSpecialStatuses[target].shellBellDmg is still 125 when state 12 runs on the OHKO KO arm (arms.ohkoKingsRock.atMoveendState11), so the HOLD_EFFECT_SHELL_BELL branch's shellBellDmg gates (src/battle_util.c:3789-3790) hold on a KO exactly as on a survive. Shell Bell spends no Random() in any case; its only remaining gate is `gBattleMons[gBattlerAttacker].hp != gBattleMons[gBattlerAttacker].maxHP` (:3792), which is orthogonal to the KO. NOT staged live here: an attacker already below max HP needs a two-turn fixture, which this bounded step did not have room for -- see ISSUES #129's trimmed remainder."
  },
  "engineVerdict": {
    "status": "NOT DIVERGENT",
    "what": "src/engine/battleScriptMoveEndOpcode.ts:883-905 draws once at MOVEEND_KINGSROCK_SHELLBELL whenever battleMoveDamage != 0, the attacker holds a HOLD_EFFECT_FLINCH item, the target took physical/special damage and NO_EFFECT is clear -- the ROM's own draw-before-flag order. That is exactly the three-draw OHKO hit the ROM produces. No engine change was made for #129.",
    "supersedes": "tools/probe/receipts/gate6-ohko-off.json's engineDivergence block and kingsRockControl block, both of which were window-truncated. That receipt has been corrected in the same commit."
  },
  "assertions": [
